  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-04T13:55:48.765Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "TL;DR: Certain new CPU architectures perform much worse in DirectX 11 (VRChat default) engine. DirectX 12 VR support would help expand support to mixed computer setups along with old and new computer architectures. DirectX 11 bottlenecks and hinders the performance of new systems excessively, and DirectX 12 does not.\n\n\n I encountered this issue after I upgraded my motherboard and CPU to a high-tier model. What I ended up with was extremely poor framerates only on the VRChat build because of some errors in DirectX 11 support. I reinstalled windows twice in both versions. The last attempt to try to fix the framerate issue was to force DirectX 12, and, to my surprise, my framerate doubled, and I was no longer stuck at 100% constant GPU usage locked at 45 fps in a world with no players. Unfortunately, DirectX 12 doesn't support VR natively on VRChat and will only boot on PC, adding support to VR for DirectX 12 would be beneficial for the future of VRChat and would solve my framerate issue which now makes VRChat unplayable for me.",
